item 0 will be written off at 12 per unit. But extra sales plus avoided penalties earn about 25 per unit, so this probably comes out on top.\n- **Candidate 0:** about 1,446 units, almost exactly mean demand. A solid plan.\n- **Candidate 4:** about 1,515 units of item 0, a little more than candidate 0. Item 1 is ordered every 4 days (no extra fees, since it rides on item 0 order days). That adds about 200 in item 1 holding. Close to candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 2:** about 1,419 units and enough item 1. Probably about 240 behind candidate 0 because of the 3-day cycle.\n- **Candidate 7:** about 1,450 units and closely tracks daily demand. Behind on fees, but more stable when demand varies.\n- **Candidate 5:** about 1,294 units, roughly 150 short, and item 1 is also short. That is roughly 950 worse than candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 6:** a 3-day cycle and also short on both items (about 1,317 of item 0, 494 of item 1).\n- **Candidate 1:** a 4-day cycle with about 1,214 units of item 0, a large shortfall. Clearly the worst.\n\n**Conclusion:** I'm fairly confident 3, 0 and 4 are in the top half. The fourth place is between 2 and 7, and they are close. Candidates 5, 6 and 1 are most likely in the bottom half."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5056, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5056}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:32:36.256Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWDYSJErC3gvzTcNTNT2"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "too